  <div class="meta-box">
    <strong>Category:</strong> Recommendations & Activities<br/>
    <strong>Target Keyword:</strong> best things to do in santorini 2027<br/>
    <strong>Meta Description:</strong> Escape the tourist bottlenecks. Detailed guide to the 10 best things to do in Santorini for 2027, complete with locations, transit routes, hours, and ticket prices.<br/>
    <strong>Word Count:</strong> ~1450 words | <strong>Reading Time:</strong> 7 min read
  </div>
  <div style="text-align: center; margin: 15pt 0;"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," style="max-width: 600px; height: auto; border-radius: 6px;" /><p style="font-size: 9pt; color: #777; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; margin-top: 4pt;">Featured Image: ammoudi_bay_waterfront___color_1794487458635.jpg</p></div>
  <p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">
    <h1 style="color: #0b4f6c; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 26pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;">Beyond Oia's Crowds: 10 Best Things to Do & Hidden Gems in Santorini (2027)</h1></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">While Oia captures headlines with its whitewashed churches and dramatic caldera cliffs, seasoned travelers know that Santorini's authentic magic often lies well outside the main tourist drag. If you want to experience the soul of the island away from cruise-ship bottlenecks, here are 10 top recommendations and hidden gems for 2027—complete with exact logistics, costs, and transit instructions.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><h2 style="color: #01baef; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; padding-bottom: 4pt;">1. Hike the Iconic Caldera Trail from Fira to Oia</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">- <strong>📍 Where:</strong> Trailhead begins in Fira behind the Catholic Cathedral, passing through Firostefani and Imerovigli to Oia Castle.
- <strong>🕒 When:</strong> Start between <strong>06:30 AM and 07:30 AM</strong>. Trek takes 3 to 4 hours (10.2 km).
- <strong>🚌 How to Get There:</strong> Walk to the trailhead if staying in Fira. If staying in Oia, take the morning KTEL bus to Fira and hike north back to Oia.
- <strong>💶 Pricing:</strong> <strong>Free</strong> public hiking trail.
- <strong>💡 Insider Tip:</strong> Always hike from <strong>Fira to Oia</strong>, never the reverse! This keeps the rising morning sun behind you and concludes in Oia just in time for an early lunch before crowds peak.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><h2 style="color: #01baef; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; padding-bottom: 4pt;">2. Step Back in Time at Akrotiri Prehistoric City</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">- <strong>📍 Where:</strong> Southwestern tip of Santorini, near Akrotiri village.
- <strong>🕒 When:</strong> Open daily 08:30 – 15:30 (summer hours extend to 20:00). Best window: 09:00 – 11:00 AM.
- <strong>🚌 How to Get There:</strong> Take the direct KTEL bus from Fira bus station to 'Akrotiri' (€2.00, runs every 45–60 minutes, 25-minute journey). The bus drops you 200 meters from the site entrance.
- <strong>💶 Pricing:</strong> <strong>€12.00</strong> regular adult admission (€6.00 reduced for EU seniors/students). Guided licensed tours available on-site for ~€15/person in small groups.
- <strong>💡 What to Expect:</strong> Often called Greece's Pompeii, this 3,600-year-old Bronze Age Minoan city was preserved in volcanic ash. Suspended walkways allow you to explore multi-story stone mansions and intact ceramic storage jars protected beneath an eco-climatic roof.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><h2 style="color: #01baef; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; padding-bottom: 4pt;">3. Explore Medieval Pyrgos and Megalochori</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">- <strong>📍 Where:</strong> The central hills of Santorini (Pyrgos is the highest village; Megalochori sits in the southwestern plain).
- <strong>🕒 When:</strong> Best in late afternoon (17:00 – 21:00) for sunset strolls and authentic dining.
- <strong>🚌 How to Get There:</strong> KTEL buses heading from Fira towards Perissa stop at both villages (€2.00, 15 minutes). Ample free municipal parking lots exist outside both pedestrian zones.
- <strong>💶 Pricing:</strong> Free exploration. Traditional meals at village tavernas cost <strong>€15–€25 per person</strong> (less than half the price of Oia restaurants).
- <strong>💡 Highlights:</strong> Pyrgos is crowned by a 13th-century Venetian castle (<em>Kasteli</em>) with panoramic 360-degree island views. Megalochori features picturesque bell towers, pirate-hideaway passages, and centuries-old wine caves (<em>kanaves</em>).</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><h2 style="color: #01baef; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; padding-bottom: 4pt;">4. Book a Sunset Caldera Catamaran Cruise</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">- <strong>📍 Where:</strong> Departs from Vlychada Marina or Ammoudi Bay.
- <strong>🕒 When:</strong> 14:30 / 15:00 departure, returning at dusk (~20:30).
- <strong>🚌 How to Get There:</strong> High-quality catamaran operators (e.g., Sunset Oia, Spiridakos) provide <strong>complimentary roundtrip hotel shuttle transfers</strong> from anywhere on the island.
- <strong>💶 Pricing:</strong> <strong>€120 – €180 per person</strong> for semi-private tours (capped at 16–20 guests). Includes unlimited Greek wine, open bar, Greek BBQ dinner, and snorkeling gear.
- <strong>💡 Why It's Worth It:</strong> Avoids the suffocating crowd at Oia Castle while offering a front-row, sea-level sunset view with volcanic hot springs swimming and Red Beach snorkeling.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><h2 style="color: #01baef; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; padding-bottom: 4pt;">5. Catch a Film at Cine Kamari (Open-Air Cinema)</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;">- <strong>📍 Where:</strong> Kamari village entrance road (directly opposite the local campsite).
- <strong>🕒 When:</strong> Nightly from May through October. Doors open at 20:30; screenings begin at 21:30.
- <strong>🚌 How to Get There:</strong> KTEL bus from Fira to Kamari (€1.80, 20 minutes; bus stop is a 4-minute walk from cinema). Taxis cost approx €25 from Fira.
- <strong>💶 Pricing:</strong> <strong>€9.00</strong> ticket price. Drinks at the bar (cocktails, local volcanic wine) are reasonably priced at €8–€12.
- <strong>💡 Experience:</strong> Voted among the top open-air cinemas in the world. Watch blockbuster movies in original English with Greek subtitles surrounded by flowering bougainvillea and moonlit pine trees.</p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><h2 style="color: #01baef; font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #e0e0e0; padding-bottom: 4pt;">Logistics Overview: Top Activities At a Glance</h2></p><p style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><tr><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Activity</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Village Location</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Transit Route</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Entry Cost</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Ideal Timing</td></tr>
<tr><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">:<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">:<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">:<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">:<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">:<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #dcdcdc; margin: 15pt 0;" /></td></tr>
<tr><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;"><strong>Caldera Hike</strong></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Fira to Oia</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Walk / KTEL Bus</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Free</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">06:30–10:30 AM</td></tr>
<tr><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;"><strong>Akrotiri Ruins</strong></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Akrotiri (South)</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">KTEL Bus (€2.00)</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">€12.00</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">09:00–11:00 AM</td></tr>
<tr><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;"><strong>Pyrgos & Megalochori</strong></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Central Interior</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">KTEL Bus (€2.00)</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Free</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">17:00–21:00 PM</td></tr>
<tr><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;"><strong>Catamaran Cruise</strong></td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Vlychada Marina</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">Free Hotel Shuttle</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">€120–€180</td><td style="border: 1px solid #dddddd; padding: 6pt 8pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt;">14:30–20:30 PM</td></tr>
